	(text "Assumed 4v3 reference, actually should use 1v5 reference to get best sampling of current up to 1.5A.\nCurrently R1=2.2k, R2=10K, --> 4.26V assuming 4v3 refrence\n\nTo make input voltage in a better range, for 1v5 reference must add resistor in series with R1, at +5V.\n\nR1=25, R2=10K  gives at 5.2V in (to allow margin) \n--> 10 / (25 + 10) * 5 = 1.49V\n\nCurrently R1 = 2.2k, R2 = 10K, need an extra 23k R1\n\n2 x 47k SMD Resistors in parallel will give 23k that can go in series on red wire.\n\nactual R1 is 1.9K\n\nR1 = 1.9 + 22 = 24 \nR2 = 10k\n\nOut = 10 / (10+24) * 5 = 1.47V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.07 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a59422eb-81ca-425a-bb60-1da11c4544c8")
	)
	(text_box "Lantern:\n\nArduino Nano Every 5V\n			Big red switch\nGPIO 4		Reed Switch for power off/on - REED2_SWITCH_SIDE_EDGE_POWER_OFF_ON_GPIO\n				Normally Open, closes to GND\nGPIO 5		Reed Switch for power cycle - REED1_CLOSURE_EDGE_REBOOT_GPIO\n				Normally Open, closes to GND\nGPIO 6		Neopixel ring - LED_PIN, VCC of 5V and GND - resistor of 470 Ohm\nGPIO 15		Relay, with diode and NPN MOSFET - normally closed\nGPIO D0		Serial TX to Mako, with voltage divider to logic level match to 3V3\nGPIO D1		Serial RX from Mako\nGPIO A6		Current Meter - current analog input GPIO\nGPIO A7		Current Meter - voltage analog input (VCC divided by 2)\nGPIO 18 SDA	I2C Temp and Humidity Sensor and Current Sensor\nGPIO 19 SCL	I2C Temp and Humidity Sensor and Current Sensor\nGPIO ??		Leak sensor (blue sensors) - not installed\nGPIO ??		On/Off Switch to suppress leaks - not installed\nPIN 2 		+3V3 OUT\nPIN 3		AREF\n\n\nVoltage for I2C devices: 3V3\n\nAdafruit AHT20 Temp/Humidity sensor\n* I2C Address: 0x38\n\nAdafruit INA219 Current Sensor\nhttps://www.analog.com/en/products/max471.html\n* I2C \n\nResistors and Caps\n\nNeopixel current limiting resistor of 470 Ohms on GPIO 6.\n1000uF 16V capacitor across VCC and GND on Arduino.\n10KOhm GPIO 6 to prevent float GPIO at powerup causing bright flash / inrush.\nVoltage Divide on TX output to Lemon.\n\n	GPIO D0\n	   |\n	  1KOhm\n	   |\n	   -------- TX at 3v3 to Lemon\n	  2Kohm\n	   |\n	  ----  GND\n\n\nJST 2 pin PH? Connector for TX/RX\n\nComponents on Relay board:\n\n- Panasoic ALQ05 Relay, 5V coil energisation, normally closed\n- Diode 1N4148 in reverse bias across relay coil (coil is 80mA when activated which causes it to Open)\n- Resistor 200 ohm - Gate to GPIO\n- Resistor 10K - Gate to GND\n- NPN Source to GND\n- NPN Drain to Relay (-) and positive terminal of diode\n- Relay (+) to 5V and negative terminal of diode\n- MMFTN3402 NPN MOSFET, surface mount\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 12.7 0)
		(size 80.01 134.62)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "433bdb5b-6dbf-4639-be7f-3fa5fb4dc21f")
	)
	(text_box "Neopixel ring:\n\nGPIO D6\nD6 --> 10k --> GND  (pulls low at power on to \n					prevent inrush of bright flash of all LEDs)\nD6 --> 477 Ohms --> NEOPIXEL DATA LINE\n\nAcross 5V and GND - 16V 1000uF capacitor\nUART TX Arduino 5V --> 2K Ohm --> TX 3.3V Logic High ESP32-S3 --> 1K Ohm --> GND\n\n2 Reeds down to GND from their GPIOs.\n\nFrom Power Bank:\n\n5V --> 3 Amp fuse --> V+ of Current Sensor --> V- of current sensor --> Switch --> Input \nof relay --> output of relay --> 5V lemon power --> Lemon --> GND\n\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 95.25 12.7 0)
		(size 46.99 100.33)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
